course: dictionary
lesson: 1535
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. A certificate can be an official paper that proves something, a prize for doing well, or the age rating of a film. «The certificate is nice, but what matters is what she does next» is about a prize, because the writer is talking about swimming and helping a friend.
explain: «Chloe's sister came home with a gold certificate for spelling.» The words for spelling are the clue: this is a prize paper for good work. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then put it into the sentence to check.
explain: Official certificates are different. A birth certificate proves when and where you were born, so families keep it safe. A qualification is a certificate showing you have learned something, like an exam pass that you can show to a future boss.
fact: A certificate can be an official paper that proves something is true.
fact: A birth certificate proves when and where a person was born.
fact: A certificate can also be a prize paper given for an achievement, like a star-of-the-week certificate.
fact: In films, a certificate is the age rating, such as PG or 12, which tells parents which ages a film suits.
fact: Useful phrases: get a certificate, award a certificate, a PG certificate.
exercise: «Chloe's sister came home with a gold certificate for spelling.» What kind of certificate is this? | *A prize paper for good work | A film's age rating | A passport | A birth certificate
exercise: What does a birth certificate prove? | How tall a baby is | *When and where a person was born | That someone can swim | That a film is for adults
exercise: A film has the certificate 12. What does this tell you? | Who made the film | How many stars it has | How long the film lasts | *Which ages the film suits
test: «The certificate is nice, but what matters is what she does next: swims safely, helps a friend.» Is the certificate here a prize? | No, it is a house paper | No, it is a film rating | No, it is a birth certificate | *Yes, a prize for swimming
test: Which certificate would a family keep safe for many years? | A star-of-the-week certificate | *A birth certificate | A swimming badge | A certificate for a school trip
exam: «A qualification is a certificate showing you have learned something.» What does certificate mean here? | A big house | *A paper that shows you have learned something | A film rating | A type of sticker
